---
/**
 * The old address of „Lucrarea mea”.
 *
 * The screen was named after the paperwork — the request — because at the time
 * that was all it held. It now holds the thesis: the title, the deadlines, the
 * file itself. Somebody a month from defending does not go looking for „cererile
 * mele”.
 *
 * The address stays alive because it is written in emails already delivered, in
 * bookmarks and in the notifications sent so far, exactly as `/profesor/arhiva`
 * is kept. 301 with the query intact: the catalogue hands out links of the form
 * `?coordonator=<id>&tema=<id>`, and losing the query would drop somebody onto
 * a generic page with the topic they clicked silently gone.
 */
return Astro.redirect(`/lucrarea-mea${Astro.url.search}`, 301)
---
